 :reading
 "The seven fundamentals are not seven independent gaps. Six of them are the input list of the seventh: Q(o|pi) = A composed with B^pi applied to the belief, scored against C, over a policy index pi, and the census found that pi (:machine-policy-carrier), B at the controlled grain (:controlled-transition-kernel), the belief-to-state map (:belief-to-state-distribution), the intermediate Q(s|pi) (:policy-conditioned-state-predictive) and C at outcome grain (:machine-preference-distribution) are each missing on both sides. That is why the Q constructor has stayed missing through repeated audits: it is not one declaration that nobody wrote, it is a composition whose every argument is absent at the required grain. The parameter kernels are a second cluster, hanging off canonical EIG rather than off risk. THE ORDER THIS IMPLIES: name pi, then map belief into the model's state, then make B carry the action, and Q is then a definition rather than a research problem -- which is the order Q-interface-completeness.edn :work-order already gives, now with the reason for each step measured."

 :derivation-proposal
 {:goal "This file is hand-kept. The ruling asks that the F-list be DERIVED from the Lean model. Proposed mechanism, NOT IMPLEMENTED here (F0 changes no code)."
  :what-lean-cannot-do
  "Lean cannot decide that a signature is uninhabited, and the corpus proves the point: every carrier in the spine already has a fixture value, and Nonempty of a function type follows from an inhabited codomain. So a fundamental cannot be a computed property of the model. It must be a DECLARED OBLIGATION carried by the model, with machine-checkable parts."
  :field-that-would-carry-the-marker
  {:where "mathlib4/DarkTower/Contract/Emit.lean:13-24, structure Declaration"
   :add "one field, constructorObligation : Option String, holding the required constructing signature verbatim; emitted as constructor-obligation by Declaration.toJson (mathlib4/DarkTower/Contract/Emit.lean:39-47)."
   :reuse "TWO FIELDS FOR THIS ALREADY EXIST AND ARE EMPTY: clojureLocus and fixture are declared on Declaration (mathlib4/DarkTower/Contract/Emit.lean:20-21) and are null on ALL 124 rows of the current holes-contract.json (counted). clojureLocus should carry the runtime seam (the :runtime :seam-read pointer of each entry above) and fixture should carry the value that must NOT count as an inhabitant. No new field is needed for either leg."
   :do-not "Do NOT add a third DeclarationKind. lean_state_probe.bb:238 partitions on kind = hole, so a third value would silently drop these rows out of both the hole count and the closed count. Fundamentals stay kind := .hole and are distinguished by their minting constructor."}
  :minting
  {:where "mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean, beside mkHole (:7747-7750)"
   :add "private def mkFundamental (name owner signature clojureLocus fixture evidence falsifier : String) : Declaration, setting kind := .hole and the three fields above."
   :why-this-shape "The probe already learns the hole-minting constructors FROM SOURCE rather than hard-coding them (lean_state_probe.bb:242-248 regexes every private def whose body matches kind := .hole; its own comment says a third could be added), and records each hole with the constructor that minted it (:253-258, :source-holes carries {:name :constructor}). So the fundamentals list is derivable from the EXISTING probe output the day mkFundamental lands: filter :source-holes on :constructor = mkFundamental."}
  :what-consumes-it
  [{:consumer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/lean_state_probe.bb:237-258,386-400"
    :change "add :contract-fundamentals derived from the JSON exactly as :contract-holes is (:237-238), plus the same two-way reconciliation as :in-source-not-in-contract / :in-contract-not-in-source (:394-395), so an emission that has drifted from the source is REPORTED rather than trusted."}
   {:consumer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/build_step.bb"
    :change "the :F priority reads the derived list; a fundamental with no open :F row is a finding the loop can raise, which is the operational form of stop other work until this is solved."}
   {:consumer "this file"
    :change "FUNDAMENTALS.edn :entries becomes the NEGATIVE CONTROL rather than the source: the derived set must equal the recorded set, and a disagreement is the finding. Hand-kept content survives only as the :lean/:runtime reading behind each entry, which no emission can carry."}]
  :three-checkable-parts
  ["(a) The companion obligation is still open: each fundamental gets a Prop declaration whose body is sorry, so the probe's existing :holes-without-a-sorry lint (lean_state_probe.bb:397-400) reads it, and discharging the fundamental by writing the constructor flips the emission without anyone editing a list."
   "(b) The named fixture is still the only value of the carrier type in the corpus -- a countable check over the module list, which is what this census did by hand."
   "(c) clojure-locus resolves as a file:line pointer, under the u56_pointer_check.bb convention."]
  :what-it-still-cannot-check "That the runtime object at clojure-locus is a PROXY rather than an inhabitant. That judgement is the reading recorded per entry above, and it is the part a human or a review has to make; the emission can carry it, not decide it."
